# Accessors and Mutators

## 1. Lesson Goals

By the end of this lesson, students should be able to:

- explain what an **accessor** method is
- explain what a **mutator** method is
- identify getter and setter methods in Java code
- explain why accessors and mutators are used with private attributes
- write getter methods that return private attribute values
- write setter methods that update private attributes safely
- add validation inside setter methods
- distinguish read-only, write-only, and read-write attributes
- trace how setter calls change object state
- answer exam-style questions about getters, setters, and encapsulation

