## 5. Real-life Example

### Example: Student Mark

A student's mark should be protected.

Poor design:

```java
s1.mark = 150;
```

Problem:

```text
150 is not a valid mark
```

Better design:

```java
s1.setMark(85);
System.out.println(s1.getMark());
```

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `getMark()` | returns the current mark |
| `setMark(int mark)` | changes the mark only if it is valid |

::: info Scenario Link
The outside program can still interact with the object, but it must follow the rules defined inside the class.
:::

