## 16. Complete Student Class

```java
public class Student {
    private String studentId;
    private String name;
    private int mark;

    public Student(String studentId, String name, int mark) {
        this.studentId = studentId;
        this.name = name;
        setMark(mark);
    }

    public String getStudentId() {
        return studentId;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public int getMark() {
        return mark;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        if (name.length() > 0) {
            this.name = name;
        }
    }

    public void setMark(int mark) {
        if (mark >= 0 && mark <= 100) {
            this.mark = mark;
        }
    }

    public boolean hasPassed() {
        return mark >= 50;
    }
}
```

### Design Explanation

| Attribute | Access Control | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `studentId` | getter only | ID should not change |
| `name` | getter + setter | name can be corrected |
| `mark` | getter + validated setter | mark must remain 0-100 |

