## 18. `this` in Setters

Setters often use parameter names that match attribute names.

```java
private int mark;

public void setMark(int mark) {
    this.mark = mark;
}
```

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `this.mark` | the object's attribute |
| `mark` | the parameter received by the method |

Without `this`, this code is wrong:

```java
public void setMark(int mark) {
    mark = mark;
}
```

It assigns the parameter to itself and does not change the attribute.

::: warning Common Mistake
Use `this.attributeName` when the parameter has the same name as the attribute.
:::

