## 20. Common Mistakes

| Mistake | Why it is a problem | Better habit |
|---|---|---|
| Getter has `void` return type | It cannot return the value | Getter return type should match attribute |
| Setter returns a value unnecessarily | Setter usually updates state only | Use `void` unless there is a clear reason |
| Setter has no validation | Invalid values may still be stored | Validate important values |
| Providing setter for every attribute | Some data should be read-only | Only add setters when changes are allowed |
| Returning wrong attribute | Getter gives incorrect data | Check return statement |
| `mark = mark;` in setter | Parameter assigned to itself | Use `this.mark = mark;` |
| Making attributes public and also writing setters | Encapsulation is weakened | Keep attributes private |
| Forgetting to call setter in constructor | Constructor may skip validation | Use `setMark(mark)` when suitable |
| Using getter to change data | Getter should read data only | Use setter or another method |
| Not checking String length | Empty names may be accepted | Validate text input where needed |

