## 26. One-page Revision Summary

| Point | Summary |
|---|---|
| Accessor | Method that reads private data |
| Getter | Common name for accessor |
| Mutator | Method that changes private data |
| Setter | Common name for mutator |
| Getter pattern | `public Type getName() { return name; }` |
| Setter pattern | `public void setName(Type name) { this.name = name; }` |
| Validation | Check new value before assigning it |
| Read-only attribute | Getter but no setter |
| Controlled access | Outside code uses methods, not direct attribute access |
| `this` | Refers to current object's attribute |
| Encapsulation link | Private attributes + public accessors/mutators |
| Common mistake | Writing `mark = mark;` instead of `this.mark = mark;` |
| Exam phrase | Accessors and mutators provide controlled access to private attributes |

